{"author":"Unknown","author_email":"","data":{"content_hash":"d4f81c4fe9adc661d6e24f5e8026d19dfb0b96525cb3a68e5cc06ce10574e5da","digest":{"component_or_area":"test suite / rebar_reconciler","key_entities":["tests/integration/rebar_reconciler/test_post_deletion_smoke.py","tests/unit/test_silent_success.py","tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/orchestrate/test_health_baseline.py","test_post_deletion_smoke","test_repair_json_receives_schema","test_capture_baseline_not_implemented_error_not_raised","parse_structured","tolerant_parse","json_repair.repair_json"],"problem_keywords":["test quality","test hygiene","smoke test","schema-guided parsing","redundant test","test coverage","linkage detection"],"propositions":["The post-deletion smoke test is mislabeled; it tests stale-import/linkage detection but is positioned as proving every leaf is invocable.","test_repair_json_receives_schema asserts schema forwarding as a kwarg without demonstrating that schema guidance changes the parsed result.","test_capture_baseline_not_implemented_error_not_raised is redundant, asserting only 'is not None' when stronger neighboring baseline tests exist.","Schema-guided parsing needs a concrete behavioral test showing parse_structured coerces string 'count' to integer 3 while tolerant_parse without schema preserves it as string.","The renamed smoke test should scope its docstring and coverage note to linkage-detection only, preferring module import resolution over pretend-execution of leaves."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-bafc-eca40294bec2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1785818869345128056,"uuid":"7af70817-c19c-465d-b2b9-89d608f52e39"}